{"name":"Le Corbusier Crush","hex":"#bf4e46","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"crush","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A violent collision or compression; a crash; destruction; ruin.","Violent pressure, as of a moving crowd."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To press between two hard objects; to squeeze so as to alter the natural shape or integrity, or to force together into a mass.","To reduce to fine particles by pounding or grinding."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crush"}],"entries":[{"title":"Le Corbusier","blocks":[{"text":"Charles-Édouard Jeanneret, known as Le Corbusier, was a French-Swiss architectural designer, painter, urban planner and writer who is described as one of the pioneers of what is now regarded as modern architecture. He was born in Switzerland to French-speaking Swiss parents and acquired French nationality in 1930. He designed buildings in Europe, Japan, India, and the Americas during a five-decade career. He considered that \"the roots of modern architecture are to be found in Viollet-le-Duc.\""}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Le_Corbusier_%281964%29.jpg/330px-Le_Corbusier_%281964%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Le_Corbusier","wikidata":"Q4724"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/bd/Le_Corbusier_%28Charles-%C3%89douard_Jeanneret%29%2C_1920%2C_Still_Life%2C_oil_on_canvas%2C_80.9_x_99.7_cm%2C_Museum_of_Modern_Art.jpg/330px-Le_Corbusier_%28Charles-%C3%89douard_Jeanneret%29%2C_1920%2C_Still_Life%2C_oil_on_canvas%2C_80.9_x_99.7_cm%2C_Museum_of_Modern_Art.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/bd/Le_Corbusier_%28Charles-%C3%89douard_Jeanneret%29%2C_1920%2C_Still_Life%2C_oil_on_canvas%2C_80.9_x_99.7_cm%2C_Museum_of_Modern_Art.jpg/330px-Le_Corbusier_%